@lang en
-- Tests of ie-citation-and-text.l4: s 7(1)(a), (b), (c); s 14(2); s 14(3); s 15(2).
-- Expected values were decided from the text of each provision (quoted in the comments) and never from the code.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`
IMPORT `ie-citation-and-text`

§ `Section 7(1): the text a court may use for the purposes of section 5 or 6`

-- (a) in the case of an Act of the Oireachtas, the signed text of such law as enrolled for record in the Office of the Registrar of the Supreme Court pursuant to Article 25.4.5° of the Constitution
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` EQUALS `the text that section 7(1)(a) names`
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` EQUALS `the signed text as enrolled for record in the Office of the Registrar of the Supreme Court pursuant to Article 25.4.5 of the Constitution`
-- (b) in the case of an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstát Éireann, the signed text of such law as enrolled for record in the office of such officer of the Supreme Court of Saorstát Éireann as Dáil Éireann determined pursuant to Article 42 of the Constitution of the Irish Free State
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` EQUALS `the text that section 7(1)(b) names`
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` EQUALS `the signed text as enrolled for record in the office of the officer of the Supreme Court of Saorstat Eireann whom Dail Eireann determined pursuant to Article 42 of the Constitution of the Irish Free State`
-- (c) in the case of any other Act, such text of that Act as corresponds to the text of the Act enrolled in the manner referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `any other Act, paragraph (c)` EQUALS `the text that section 7(1)(c) names`
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `any other Act, paragraph (c)` EQUALS `such text of the Act as corresponds to the text enrolled in the manner referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)`
-- the three paragraphs name three different texts
#ASSERT NOT (`the text that section 7(1)(a) names` EQUALS `the text that section 7(1)(b) names`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the text that section 7(1)(b) names` EQUALS `the text that section 7(1)(c) names`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the text that section 7(1)(a) names` EQUALS `the text that section 7(1)(c) names`)
-- the court may make use of the matter when it is construing for section 5 or 6 and the matter accompanies and is set out in the text named for that kind of Act
-- arguments: the kind of Act; the court is construing for the purposes of section 5 or 6; the matter accompanies and is set out in the named text
#ASSERT     `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `any other Act, paragraph (c)` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `any other Act, paragraph (c)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `any other Act, paragraph (c)` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` `any other Act, paragraph (c)` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 14(2): "as amended (including as amended by way of extension, application, adaptation or other modification of the enactment), whether the amendment is made before, on or after the date on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation"`

-- when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation (arguments: the day of the change; the day the citing provision came into operation)
#ASSERT `when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation` (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation` (YMD 2026 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
-- every way of changing, at every time of change, is read into the citation
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` amendment `, the change being made` `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` amendment `, the change being made` `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` amendment `, the change being made` `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` extension `, the change being made` `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` extension `, the change being made` `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` extension `, the change being made` `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` application `, the change being made` `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` application `, the change being made` `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` application `, the change being made` `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` adaptation `, the change being made` `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` adaptation `, the change being made` `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` adaptation `, the change being made` `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` `another modification` `, the change being made` `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` `another modification` `, the change being made` `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
#ASSERT `a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` `another modification` `, the change being made` `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`

§ `Section 14(3): "a comma immediately before a reference to a year and a comma immediately after such a reference that is not required for the purpose of punctuation may be omitted"`

-- arguments: what is cited; where the comma stands; whether the comma is required for the purpose of punctuation
-- F39: the qualifier is read as governing both commas
#ASSERT     `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `an Act, by its short title` `immediately before a reference to a year` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `an Act, by its short title` `immediately before a reference to a year` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `an Act, by its short title` `immediately after a reference to a year` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `an Act, by its short title` `immediately after a reference to a year` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `an Act, by its short title` `elsewhere` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `an Act, by its short title` `elsewhere` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `another enactment, by its citation` `immediately before a reference to a year` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `another enactment, by its citation` `immediately before a reference to a year` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `another enactment, by its citation` `immediately after a reference to a year` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `another enactment, by its citation` `immediately after a reference to a year` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `another enactment, by its citation` `elsewhere` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `another enactment, by its citation` `elsewhere` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `something else, or in some other way` `immediately before a reference to a year` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `something else, or in some other way` `immediately before a reference to a year` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `something else, or in some other way` `immediately after a reference to a year` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `something else, or in some other way` `immediately after a reference to a year` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `something else, or in some other way` `elsewhere` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` `something else, or in some other way` `elsewhere` TRUE

§ `Section 15(2): the Clerk of Dail Eireann endorses the date of the passing, and that date is taken to be part of the Act`

-- the date to be endorsed is the date of the passing, which is the day the Bill is signed by the President (s 15(1))
#ASSERT `the date the Clerk of Dail Eireann must endorse on the Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the date the Clerk of Dail Eireann must endorse on the Act` (YMD 2005 10 17) EQUALS YMD 2005 10 17
-- the date endorsed is the date of the passing: it is taken to be part of the Act
#ASSERT `the endorsed date is taken to be part of the Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))
#ASSERT `the endorsed date is taken to be part of the Act` (YMD 2005 10 17) (JUST (YMD 2005 10 17))
-- nothing endorsed: nothing is deemed part of the Act
#ASSERT NOT `the endorsed date is taken to be part of the Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) NOTHING
-- a different date endorsed: the section does not say
#ASSERT REFUSED `the endorsed date is taken to be part of the Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 11)) BECAUSE "section 15(2) deems the date of the passing to be part of the Act and does not say what follows if a different date is endorsed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the endorsed date is taken to be part of the Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 9)) BECAUSE "section 15(2) deems the date of the passing to be part of the Act and does not say what follows if a different date is endorsed"
-- F43: "Immediately after": the text gives no measure of time
#ASSERT REFUSED `the latest moment by which the Clerk of Dail Eireann must have endorsed the date` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "section 15(2) says immediately and gives no measure of time"
